,"commission_lane":["DMC","package","event"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Machu Picchu?","a":"Altitude, not crime. Cusco sits at ~3,400 m and acute mountain sickness (*soroche*) is the primary health risk — headache, nausea, breathlessness. Acclimatize in the lower Sacred Valley (~2,800 m) before Cusco or any trek, ascend gradually, and rest day one; the citadel itself (2,430 m) is lower, so many feel better there.","source":"alpacaexpeditions.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":""},{"q":"How hard is the Inca Trail, and do I need a guide?","a":"You cannot legally hike the classic trail without a licensed guide, and it is demanding, not casual. Only 500 permits are issued per day (~200 hikers), the trail closes every February, and the Day-2 crux is Dead Woman''s Pass at 4,215 m — a ~1,200 m ascent where oxygen is ~60% of sea level. Book 4–7 months ahead for peak.","source":"incatrail.org / machupicchusoul.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is the Huayna Picchu climb dangerous?","a":"It''s exposed but managed — bookable for the sure-footed. Huayna Picchu is a ~2-hour climb capped at 400 permits/day, with big drop-offs, narrow original Inca stairs and cable-assisted sections; it is not for those uneasy with heights. Machu Picchu Mountain is the longer, higher, less-exposed alternative.","source":"samtravelperu.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is the Belmond Hiram Bingham worth it for a honeymoon?","a":"For a marquee honeymoon, yes — it removes the ticket-scramble. The Hiram Bingham bundles citadel entry, bus and guide into a ~1h45m polished-brass rail run, and pairs with the Sanctuary Lodge, the only hotel at the gate (first in at dawn, last out at dusk). Hold both as early as the trek permit.","source":"belmond.com / thesouthamericaspecialists.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Machu Picchu?","a":"May–October (dry season) is best and June–August is clearest — cloudless mornings — because the wet season (Nov–March) is lusher but rainier and February closes the Inca Trail entirely. The daily citadel cap also rises to 5,600 for the Jun 19–Nov 2 high-season block, so book early.","source":"salkantaytrekking.com / bushop.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"}],"seo":{"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-07","meta_title":"Machu Picchu, Peru — When to Go, Inca Trail Permits, Tickets & Where to Stay (2026)","search_language":"es-PE","local_keywords":["Machu Picchu entradas","Camino Inca permisos","cómo llegar a Machu Picchu","boletos Machu Picchu 2026 circuitos","mal de altura Cusco soroche","tren a Machu Picchu PeruRail","Salkantay o Lares","Huayna Picchu entradas","Valle Sagrado aclimatación","Inti Raymi Cusco 24 de junio"],"hreflang":["en","es-PE"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-07","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/peru","read":"2026-08-20T14:53:51Z","source_updated":"2026-06-22T23:35:12+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Sanctuary Lodge, A Belmond Hotel","why_ultra":"Only hotel adjacent to the citadel gate — first in at dawn, last out at dusk","earning":"Belmond commission via Fora/Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"Bellini-Club perks: breakfast, credit, upgrades, priority dawn access","mor":"Hotel/DMC direct or