Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"adventure DMC / climbing-school affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","culinary":"destination","culture":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate","school"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Sumapaz páramo trek","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/articles/day-hikes-bogota-colombia","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the world''s largest páramo ecosystem, south of Bogotá; high-altitude moorland trekking, guided-only","si":"adventure","blurb":"the world''s largest páramo ecosystem, south of Bogotá; high-altitude moorland trekking, guided-only","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"GEA DMC / licensed guide (guided-only)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","culinary":"destination","culture":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Paloquemao market + coffee","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","source":"https://theabroadguide.com/la-candelaria-mount-monserrate-and-the-gold-museum-in-one-day-in-bogota/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Bogotá''s great produce, flower and food market; early-morning fruit tastings and Colombian-coffee sourcing, a food-tour anchor","si":"culinary","blurb":"Bogotá''s great produce, flower and food market; early-morning fruit tastings and Colombian-coffee sourcing, a food-tour anchor","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"food-tour affiliate + DMC","wells":["eat","activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culinary"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culinary":"primary","culture":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Andrés Carne de Res (Chía)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Restaurant_Review-g815502-d939879-Reviews-Andres_Carne_De_Res_Chia-Chia_Cundinamarca_Department.html","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the legendary maximalist restaurant ~40–60 min north of Bogotá — a labyrinth of over-the-top décor, live music and improv actors","si":"culinary","blurb":"the legendary maximalist restaurant ~40–60 min north of Bogotá — a labyrinth of over-the-top décor, live music and improv actors","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"DMC dining + vetted transport","wells":["eat"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culinary"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","culinary":"primary","culture":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the most romantic thing to do in Bogotá?","a":"Ride the funicular or cable car up Monserrate at dusk for dinner at the summit restaurant, with the whole plateau of light beneath you — the city''s signature romance run. The ridge rises to 3,152 m (10,341 ft), and the Basilica crowns the summit.","source":"kittiaroundtheworld.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you go hiking near Bogotá?","a":"Yes — Andean páramo day-hikes start on the city''s doorstep and run guided. Chingaza páramo climbs from 2,600 to 4,000 m through frailejón moorland and glacial Siecha/Buitrago lagoons, while Suesca, about 1 hour north, is Colombia''s premier rock-climbing crag. Guided entry is the norm for the páramos.","source":"mytriptocolombia.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"adventure"},{"q":"What are the must-see museums and sights in Bogotá?","a":"The Gold Museum (Museo del Oro) is the headline — ~55,000 pre-Columbian gold pieces, including the Muisca raft of the El Dorado legend, and free on Sundays — alongside the Botero Museum and colonial La Candelaria. The core clusters in and above the historic centre.","source":"viator.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Where should you eat and drink around Bogotá?","a":"Andrés Carne de Res in Chía is the marquee night out — ranked #2 of 139 restaurants in Chía, a labyrinth of over-the-top décor, live music and improv actors, about 40–60 min north of the city. In town, Zona G is Bogotá''s dense \"gourmet zone.\"","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Bogotá?","a":"Scopolamine (\"devil''s breath\" / burundanga) drugging is the headline traveler risk — a colourless, tasteless sedative used to rob or assault. Bogotá police recorded 1,409 cases in 2023 (+16% year-on-year), concentrated in Chapinero, Teusaquillo and Santa Fe, often via dating apps and offered drinks. Never accept drinks or tabs from strangers.","source":"thecitypaperbogota.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is walking up Monserrate dangerous?","a":"Walk the Monserrate pilgrimage trail only in daylight and in groups — robberies have been reported on the path — or take the funicular or cable car instead. The summit stands at 3,152 m, so pace yourself for the altitude.","source":"kittiaroundtheworld.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Bogotá & The Andes, Colombia — Gold Museum, Monserrate, Zipaquirá & Villa de Leyva | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","search_language":"es-CO","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Bogotá","Catedral de Sal Zipaquirá","Museo del Oro","Villa de Leyva","Monserrate Bogotá","hoteles de lujo Bogotá"],"hreflang":["en","es-CO"],"attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/colombia","read":"2026-08-20T14:47:41Z","source_updated":"2026-08-18T15:51:11+01:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07","long_tail":["things to do in Bogotá Colombia","Gold Museum Bogotá guide","Monserrate funicular Bogotá","Zipaquirá Salt Cathedral day trip from Bogotá","Villa de Leyva from Bogotá","is Bogotá safe 2026","Bogotá altitude sickness"]},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["romance","adventure","culture","culinary"],"ultra":[{"name":"Four Seasons Hotel Casa Medina","type":"landmark 1946 building, Zona G, 62 rooms + 19 suites, Ministry-of-Culture monument","routing":"Fora/Virtuoso preferred","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Four Seasons Hotel Bogotá","type":"second FS property, Zona T entertainment district, contemporary tower","routing":"Fora/Virtuoso preferred","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Sofitel Bogotá Victoria Regia","type":"French-luxury prestige address, northern corridor","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"luxury→ultra"},{"name":"W Bogotá (Zona T)","type":"Marriott lifestyle-luxury flagship, design-forward rooftop","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Click Clack Hotel","type":"design-forward boutique, northern corridor","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"premium→luxury"},{"name":"Zona G / Chicó luxury-apartment buyouts","type":"serviced multi-bedroom apartments w/ concierge","routing":"MoR villa + host","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Bogotá & The Andes, Colombia, Colombia"},"geo":{"lat":4.711,"lng":-74.0721},"orbit":[{"id":"medellin-colombia","jewels":8,"si":["culture"]}],"orbit_country":["cartagena-colombia","san-andres-colombia"]}'::jsonb, 12),
