ada/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Open-water small-boat operation, sun exposure, weather turns Guided only Confirm life vests on board and worn, weather-check the launch, no touching/chasing dolphins, motion-sickness prep","si":"romance","blurb":"Open-water small-boat operation, sun exposure, weather turns Guided only Confirm life vests on board and worn, weather-check the launch, no touching/chasing dolphins, motion-sickness prep","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"licensed sanctuary boat tour via affiliate (GetYourGuide/Civitatis) or DMC","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"The Malecón at sunset (7 km Gulf-front)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/mexico/yucatan-peninsula/campeche/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"romance","when":"year-round","commission":"free amenity selling boutique-hotel package","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["package","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Candlelit colonial-courtyard dining","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/cpehl-hacienda-puerta-campeche-a-luxury-collection-hotel-campeche/overview/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"hotel F&B + room commission","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Pan de cazón (state dish)","si_tag":"CUL","tier":"essential","source":"https://mexiconewsdaily.com/lifestyle/food/state-by-plate-campeches-pan-de-cazon/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Campechano cuisine is one of Mexico''s most distinct regional tables","si":"culinary","blurb":"Campechano cuisine is one of Mexico''s most distinct regional tables","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"guided food walk / cooking class (tour affiliate)","wells":["eat"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["culinary"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Pámpano en escabeche & coctel campechano","si_tag":"CUL","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/campeche-food-guide/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"curated dining list + food tour / market visit","wells":["eat"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — si (unambiguous spend type)","si_all":["culinary"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Calakmul gateway (own dossier)","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"premier","source":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/895/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the deep-jungle Maya megacity + biosphere is a long day/overnight from Campeche City and should not be collapsed into this file","si":"culture","blurb":"the deep-jungle Maya megacity + biosphere is a long day/overnight from Campeche City and should not be collapsed into this file","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"multi-day DMC program from Campeche City","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","romance":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is there to see in the walled city?","a":"The UNESCO centro itself: a 17th-century wall (1686–1704), eight bastions, a checkerboard grid and 1,000+ colonial buildings painted ochre, coral and mint — walk Calle 59 at golden hour. At night, the Puerta de Tierra sound-and-light show projects four centuries of pirate history onto the Land Gate for about US$5.","source":"whc.unesco.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Edzná worth a day trip from Campeche?","a":"Yes — it is the region''s under-visited Maya highlight. Edzná, 52 km southeast, is a major Maya capital whose five-story pyramid rises ~40 m and blends Puuc, Chenes and Petén styles, with a rare ancient hydraulic canal system and a fraction of Chichén Itzá''s crowds. Go at the 8 AM opening to beat the heat.","source":"themayanruinswebsite.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Campeche good for a couple''s trip?","a":"Yes, as a slow, characterful pause. Dinner in a restored-hacienda courtyard (La Guardia at Hacienda Puerta Campeche), a rooftop pool at an 18th-century mansion, and the peninsula''s best sunset along the 7-km malecón make it a honeymoon-adjacent \"second city,\" most often paired with Mérida (~2.5 hr) as a 2–3 night add-on.","source":"lonelyplanet.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What should I eat in Campeche?","a":"Start with pan de cazón — the state dish of layered tortillas, black beans, shredded dogfish and tomato-habanero sauce. Add pámpano en escabeche (colonial-era pompano in bitter-orange escabeche) and the coctel campechano seafood cocktail, with Gulf catch landed the same morning.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Campeche?","a":"Heat and thin flight schedules, not crime. The exposed ruins at Edzná and the treeless malecón are hot at midday — hat, high SPF, water and early site visits. Campeche''s own airport (CPE) is thinly served, so most travelers fly into Mérida (MID) and drive ~2.5 hr; drink bottled water only and use repellent for dengue in the rainy season (Jun–Oct).","source":"climatestotravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Campeche City, Mexico — The Walled UNESCO Pastel Port | TravelWell.World","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Campeche","ciudad amurallada Campeche","Edzná zona arqueológica","hoteles boutique centro histórico Campeche","avistamiento de delfines Isla Aguada","pan de cazón Campeche","Carnaval de Campeche fechas"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","primary_keyword":"Campeche City","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07","long_tail":["is Campeche City Mexico safe","things to do in Campeche walled city","Edzná ruins day trip from Campeche","Isla Aguada dolphin tour Campeche","best boutique hotels Campeche historic center"]},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"property":"Hacienda Puerta Campeche, a Luxury Collection Hotel","brand":"Marriott — Luxury Collection","rooms":14,"positioning":"Restored 16th-c. haciendas; the destination''s true luxury ceiling","earning":"Marriott commissionable; Luxury Collection eligible for Marriott STARS/Luxury consortia — verify FHR/amenity status at booking","mor":"hotel-direct commission","tier":"$$$$"},{"property":"Casa Don Gustavo Boutique Hotel","rooms":10,"positioning":"Restored 18th-c. mansion, rooftop pool, pedestrian center","earning":"Independent — direct / bedbank / consortia","mor":"hotel-direct or platform","tier":"$$$"},{"property":"Hotel H177","positioning":"Boutique centro property, Calle 59","earning":"Independent boutique; direct / affiliate","mor":"hotel-direct or platform","tier":"comfort"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Campeche City, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":19.845,"lng":-90.523},"orbit":[{"id":"calakmul-mexico","jewels":8,"si":["culture","wildlife","expedition"]}],"orbit_country":["akumal-mexico","bacalar-mexico","balandra-beach-mexico","cabo-pulmo-mexico","cabo-san-lucas-mexico","cancun-mexico","careyes-mexico","celestun-mexico","chapala-ajijic-mexico","chichen-itza-mexico","coba-mexico","costalegre-mexico","cozumel-mexico","east-cape-mexico","ensenada-mexico","espiritu-santo-island-mexico","guadalajara-mexico","guanajuato-city-mexico","holbox-mexico","huatulco-mexico","isla-contoy-mexico","isla-mujeres-mexico","izamal-mexico","la-paz-mexico","loreto-mexico","los-barriles-mexico","magdalena-bay-mexico","mahahual-mexico","mazamitla-mexico","merida-mexico","mexico-city-mexico","oaxaca-city-mexico","palenque-mexico","playa-del-carmen-mexico","puerto-aventuras-mexico","puerto-morelos-mexico","puerto-vallarta-mexico","punta-mita-mexico","rio-lagartos-mexico","san-cristobal-de-las-casas-mexico","san-jose-del-cabo-mexico","san-miguel-de-allende-mexico","san-sebastian-del-oeste-mexico","sayulita-mexico","sian-kaan-mexico","teotihuacan-mexico","tlaquepaque-mexico","todos-santos-mexico","tulum-mexico","uxmal-mexico","valladolid-mexico","valle-de-guadalupe-mexico","puerto-escondido-mexico"]}'::jsonb, 19),
  ('cancun-mexico', '10S', 'Cancún', 'Mexico', 'The gateway where a barrier reef meets a runway', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"tropical","adventure","diveglobal","ocean"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Sits on the Mesoamerican Barrier Reef, world''s 2nd-longest coral reef system","MUSA underwater museum: 470+ statues, 3.5-8 m, divable and snorkelable","World''s largest whale-shark aggregation offshore mid-May to mid-Sept (snorkel-only)","Best overall window Jan-Mar (clearest water, lowest sargassum)","Gateway hub for cenotes, Chichen Itza/Tulum, Isla Mujeres and Contoy"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Galenia + Hospiten Cancún (verify trauma status); hyperbaric via SSS Cancún / Cozumel","malaria":"none in QR tourist zones (verify); dengue precautions","yellow_fever":"none required","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00","source_country":"mexico","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"The city of Tijuana, in Baja California","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["airside transit through Tijuana airport","the Cross Border Xpress bridge linking the airport across the border","federal toll road 1D and the Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border"]},{"name":"The city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"The state of Chihuahua","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Chihuahua","the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez via federal toll road 45","federal toll road 45D between Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez","the Copper Canyon rail route and the towns immediately on it, including Creel","the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro","state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua"],"note":"The advisory also covers the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"name":"The state of Sinaloa","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán","road 32 between El Fuerte and Los Mochis","the 15D federal toll road running the length of the state","the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis and El Fuerte, and the towns immediately on it"]},{"name":"The state of Tamaulipas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo via federal toll road 85D from Monterrey","federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad Victoria and Magueyes","the area of Tamaulipas south of those highways"]},{"name":"The state of Zacatecas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"In Guanajuato: the areas south-west of road 45D","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D. (San Miguel de Allende and Guanajuato City sit outside this area.)"},{"name":"The state of Michoacán","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Morelia via federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (dry, lowest sargassum, highest price/crowds)","shoulder":"late Apr-Jun & Nov (~30-40% off, good weather)","green":"Jul-Oct (hurricane/rain, 40-60% below peak Sep-Oct)","booking_lead":"~3-4 months for Dec-Apr peak & spring break; 2-3 months off-peak","off_season_specials":"~30-40% off May-Jun & Nov shoulder; 40-60% off Sep-Oct green trough","event_peaks":["Spring Break (Mar)","whale-shark run mid-May-mid-Sept peak Jun-Aug","winter holidays late Dec"],"fire_date":"market Dec-Apr peak by ~September; push whale-shark green-season from ~March"},"jewels":[{"name":"MUSA Underwater Museum","si_tag":"diveglobal","status":"future","hook":"470+ submerged sculptures, divable by OW divers and snorkelers","bookable_category":"dive/snorkel/glass-bottom tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.bluewaterdivetravel.com/scuba-musa-isla-mujeres-cancun","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"470+ submerged sculptures, divable by OW divers and snorkelers","when":"year-round","commission":"local dive-op/DMC → Viator/GYG affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["diveglobal"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","diveglobal":"primary","ocean":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator","DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Whale-shark aggregation run","si_tag":"ocean","status":"future","hook":"snorkel the world''s largest whale-shark gathering, Jun-Aug peak","bookable_category":"boat snorkel excursion","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.islandlifemexico.com/cancun-snorkeling-diving-guide/","si":"ocean","blurb":"snorkel the world''s largest whale-shark gathering, Jun-Aug peak","commission":"DMC/operator → OTA affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["diveglobal","ocean"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","diveglobal":"evidenced","ocean":"primary","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator","DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Route of the Cenotes","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","hook":"jungle-road cenote circuit for swim/dive/zipline","bookable_category":"day tour + entry","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.islandlifemexico.com/cancun-snorkeling-diving-guide/","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"adventure","blurb":"jungle-road cenote circuit for swim/dive/zipline","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"DMC → OTA (entry = pass-through)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure","diveglobal"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","diveglobal":"evidenced","ocean":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Turtle-nesting programs (May-Sept)","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"live","hook":"green/hawksbill/loggerhead nesting + resort release programs","bookable_category":"eco/resort activity","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.islandlifemexico.com/cancun-snorkeling-diving-guide/","si":"adventure","blurb":"green/hawksbill/loggerhead nesting + resort release programs","commission":"resort/DMC (often pass-through)","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["adventure"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"primary","diveglobal":"destination","ocean":"destination","tropical":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"South Hotel Zone / Playa Mujeres (sargassum-protected)","si_tag":"tropical","status":"live","hook":"cleaner beach stretches in a heavy sargassum year","bookable_category":"hotel + transfer","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.howisthesargassum.com/blog/sargassum-june-2026-update","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","blurb":"cleaner beach stretches in a heavy sargassum year","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"all-inclusive portal → Amstar transfer → OTA","wells":["stay","move"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","diveglobal":"destination","ocean":"destination","tropical":"primary"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"}],"faq":[{"q":"What health risks should I actually plan for in Cancún?","a":"Water, mosquitoes, hurricanes and sargassum — not violent crime. Drink bottled/purified water; use repellent for dengue (no malaria in Quintana Roo tourist zones); hurricane season runs June–November with September riskiest; and sargassum peaks around July in 2026.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Will sargassum ruin the beaches in 2026?","a":"It''s a real risk in 2026 — plan location, don''t cancel. 2026 is tracking as one of the worst sargassum years on record, often peaking around July in the Riviera Maya; north Cancún and Playa Mujeres are among the more protected stretches, and Jan–March runs lowest on sargassum.","source":"howisthesargassum.com","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"When and how can I swim with whale sharks?","a":"Mid-May to mid-September, peaking June–August, on a snorkel-only boat excursion off Isla Mujeres/Holbox — the world''s largest whale-shark aggregation. It''s a green-season spike inside the low-price window, so rooms are cheaper then; life-vest, no-touch, follow-the-guide.","source":"islandlifemexico.com","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"Can beginners dive MUSA and the reef?","a":"Yes — MUSA is one of the most accessible dives anywhere. The 470+ statues sit 3.5–8 m down, shallow enough for Open Water divers, snorkelers and glass-bottom boats; no-fly-after-diving is 18–24 hours and these are shallow (≤9 m) day dives.","source":"bluewaterdivetravel.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Is Cancún good for an all-inclusive honeymoon, and where''s the top end?","a":"Yes — it''s a honeymoon engine. The Hotel Zone is dense all-inclusive inventory; the one true ultra address in Cancún proper is NIZUC (Punta Nizuc, ~15 min from the airport), with the deepest luxury bench just down-corridor in Mayakoba/Maroma (Rosewood, Banyan Tree, Maroma/Belmond).","source":"virtuoso.com","si_tag":"tropical"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cancún, Mexico: Reef, MUSA & Whale-Shark Gateway","meta_description":"Cancún sits on the world''s second-longest reef — dive MUSA, snorkel the whale-shark run, base for cenotes and Maya ruins. Best time, safety, and how to book.","slug":"cancun-mexico","primary_keyword":"Cancún diving and snorkeling","long_tail":["Cancún MUSA underwater museum","Cancún whale shark tour season","best time to visit Cancún","Cancún all-inclusive honeymoon","Cancún cenote day trip"],"search_language":"EN primary + ES-MX; page answers real ES queries restated (not machine-translated)","local_keywords":["mejor época para viajar a Cancún","buceo MUSA Cancún","tour tiburón ballena Cancún","qué hacer en Cancún cenotes","Cancún todo incluido luna de miel","temporada de sargazo Cancún","villas de lujo Riviera Maya"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX","x-default:en"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-04","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","source_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":[],"note":"MXN currency, USD widely accepted","advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-31","hits":9,"misses":13,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"tropical","name":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"live"},{"si":"diveglobal","name":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","name":"ocean","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"NIZUC Resort & Spa","why_ultra":"only true in-Cancún ultra enclave (Punta Nizuc), 274 suites/villas facing the reef","earning":"agent/consortium on application via host + Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"Virtuoso member — free upgrades + amenities","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack / Virtuoso)"},{"name":"Rosewood Mayakoba","why_ultra":"boutique ~130 lagoon/beach suites, private pools + butler, on mangrove canals","earning":"agent/consortium on application via host + Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"Virtuoso member","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack)"},{"name":"Banyan Tree Mayakoba","why_ultra":"all-villa private-pool privacy inside Mayakoba","earning":"agent/consortium on application via host + Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"Virtuoso member","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack)"},{"name":"Fairmont Mayakoba","why_ultra":"full-amenity luxury tier of the Mayakoba four","earning":"agent/consortium on application via host","virtuoso_value_add":"verify (reported NOT Virtuoso; check Accor ALL/other)","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack)"},{"name":"Chablé Maroma","why_ultra":"wellness-forward design ultra, private beach, Jorge Vallejo dining","earning":"agent/consortium on application via host + Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"verify present","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack)"},{"name":"Maroma, A Belmond Hotel","why_ultra":"legendary private-beach ultra, Belmond/LVMH tier","earning":"agent/consortium on application via host + Virtuoso","virtuoso_value_add":"Belmond typically Virtuoso — verify","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack)"},{"name":"La Casa de la Playa (by Xcaret)","why_ultra":"Xcaret''s top-tier ultra all-inclusive, adults/couples + eco-park access","earning":"agent/consortium via Xcaret trade / host on application","virtuoso_value_add":"verify","mor":"safe (commissionable-rack)"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Cancún, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":21.1619,"lng":-86.8515},"orbit":[{"id":"akumal-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["diveglobal","ocean","culture"]},{"id":"bacalar-mexico","jewels":6,"si":["tropical","wellness","adventure"]},{"id":"coba-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["culture","expedition","family"]},{"id":"cozumel-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["diveglobal","liveaboard","ocean"]},{"id":"holbox-mexico","jewels":4,"si":["expedition","romance","ocean","wildlife"]},{"id":"isla-contoy-mexico","jewels":3,"si":["expedition","ocean","wildlife"]},{"id":"isla-mujeres-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["tropical","ocean","diveglobal","adventure"]},{"id":"mahahual-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["liveaboard","diveglobal"]},{"id":"playa-del-carmen-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["romance","expedition","diveglobal","culture"]},{"id":"puerto-aventuras-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["romance","diveglobal","ocean","wildlife"]},{"id":"puerto-morelos-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["diveglobal","ocean","adventure","culinary"]},{"id":"sian-kaan-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["expedition","wildlife","tropical"]},{"id":"tulum-mexico","jewels":5,"si":["expedition","diveglobal","culture","wildlife"]}],"orbit_country":["balandra-beach-mexico","cabo-pulmo-mexico","cabo-san-lucas-mexico","calakmul-mexico","campeche-city-mexico","careyes-mexico","celestun-mexico","chapala-ajijic-mexico","chichen-itza-mexico","costalegre-mexico","east-cape-mexico","ensenada-mexico","espiritu-santo-island-mexico","guadalajara-mexico","guanajuato-city-mexico","huatulco-mexico","izamal-mexico","la-paz-mexico","loreto-mexico","los-barriles-mexico","magdalena-bay-mexico","mazamitla-mexico","merida-mexico","mexico-city-mexico","oaxaca-city-mexico","palenque-mexico","puerto-vallarta-mexico","punta-mita-mexico","rio-lagartos-mexico","san-cristobal-de-las-casas-mexico","san-jose-del-cabo-mexico","san-miguel-de-allende-mexico","san-sebastian-del-oeste-mexico","sayulita-mexico","teotihuacan-mexico","tlaquepaque-mexico","todos-santos-mexico","uxmal-mexico","valladolid-mexico","valle-de-guadalupe-mexico","puerto-escondido-mexico"]}'::jsonb, 20),
  ('careyes-mexico', '10S', 'Careyes (Costa Careyes)', 'Mexico', 'Careyes Mexico', 'live', 'verified', 'luxuryPool', 'Jalisco (Puerto Vallarta & Guadalajara)', '{"ultra","romance","ocean"}', '{}', '{"premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Founded 1968 by Gian Franco Brignone; 48-room beach hotel, 36 casitas, ~50 villas + clifftop castles with moat-like infinity pools","Villas privately owned, many rent fully staffed with private cook + daily housekeeping","Polo late-Nov->end-Apr (Agua Alta Cup at Easter, Chinese New Year tournament); Ondalinda x Careyes Nov 12-15 2026","Hosted Heidi Klum & Seal wedding; Tom Ford, Naomi Campbell, Uma Thurman have vacationed","Between PVR and Manzanillo (ZLO ~1.5-hr drive); private charters to Chamela strip CHM31 ~15 min / Chalacatepec ~40 min; Cuixmala & Las Alamandas have own airstrips"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"remote enclave; serious cases route to Manzanillo (~1.5 hr) or Puerto Vallarta (~2-4 hr); private airstrips serve medical evac; carry travel-medical + air-evac insurance","book_enabled":false,"air_access_verified":"private airstrip (Careyes/Cuixmala) + Manzanillo ZLO - flag for founder review","founder_flag":"gated resort enclaves with private airstrips - candidate ''resort-airstrip private-access'' clean-pass class; per gate test content-only until founder rules; LUX ultra moat","malaria":"low - mosquito avoidance (not prophylaxis) for Jalisco coastal lowlands below 1,000 m","dengue":"circulates (peak May-Nov) - daytime repellent","water":"bottled/purified (staffed villas provide)","hurricane":"May-Nov - trip insurance for summer/fall","remote":"minimal public services outside enclave; do NOT drive secondary roads after dark (advisory warning)","road_transfer":"PVR/Manzanillo transfers pass through non-carve-out southern Jalisco - the hold reason; private-air arrival is the founder-flag workaround","dive":"nearest hyperbaric chambers Puerto Vallarta & Manzanillo (1.5-4 hr) - conservative profiles, DAN insurance, strict no-fly interval","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-20T14:49:02Z","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00","source_country":"mexico","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely","fcdo_zones":[{"name":"The city of Tijuana, in Baja California","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["airside transit through Tijuana airport","the Cross Border Xpress bridge linking the airport across the border","federal toll road 1D and the Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border"]},{"name":"The city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"The state of Chihuahua","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Chihuahua","the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez via federal toll road 45","federal toll road 45D between Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez","the Copper Canyon rail route and the towns immediately on it, including Creel","the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro","state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua"],"note":"The advisory also covers the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"name":"The state of Sinaloa","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán","road 32 between El Fuerte and Los Mochis","the 15D federal toll road running the length of the state","the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis and El Fuerte, and the towns immediately on it"]},{"name":"The state of Tamaulipas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo via federal toll road 85D from Monterrey","federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad Victoria and Magueyes","the area of Tamaulipas south of those highways"]},{"name":"The state of Zacatecas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"In Guanajuato: the areas south-west of road 45D","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D. (San Miguel de Allende and Guanajuato City sit outside this area.)"},{"name":"The state of Michoacán","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Morelia via federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry season, polo/Ondalinda/celebrity winter season, holiday villa demand, humpbacks Dec-Mar)","shoulder":"May & late Oct (warm, quieter, between festivals)","green":"Jul-Oct (hot/humid, emerald hills, hurricane window May-Nov, softest villa availability)","event_peak":"polo late-Nov->end-Apr (Agua Alta Cup at Easter, Chinese New Year tournament); Ondalinda x Careyes Nov 12-15 2026","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"green season (Jul-Oct) villa buyouts at softer rates as private-family estate stays (turtle nesting Cuixmala) - the ''secret season''","sources":["https://www.ondalinda.com/festivals/careyes/","https://careyes.com/","https://mexiconewsdaily.com/travel/an-insiders-guide-to-the-perfect-weekend-in-costalegre/"],"fire_date":"content-only - no campaign; if founder rules private-air carve-out, open winter/polo/Ondalinda villa campaigns in spring for following Nov-Apr peak (6-12-mo villa lead)","event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year (ultra premium), Semana Santa/Easter (Agua Alta Cup polo), Chinese New Year (polo+gala), Ondalinda (mid-Nov)","booking_lead":"staffed ultra villas for Christmas-New Year/winter polo/Ondalinda book 6-12 months ahead, contracted direct on application; binding constraint is villa availability, not flights"},"jewels":[{"name":"Careyes clifftop Castles","si_tag":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Careyes reservations / villa specialist","source":"https://careyes.com/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"candy-colored castles with moat-like infinity pools cantilevered over the Pacific — the signature Careyes image","si":"ultra","blurb":"candy-colored castles with moat-like infinity pools cantilevered over the Pacific — the signature Careyes image","when":"year-round","commission":"on application","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"ocean":"destination","romance":"destination","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Cuixmala (Casa Cuixmala suites / hillside villas)","si_tag":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Cuixmala direct / luxury DMC","source":"https://www.luxurylatinamerica.com/mexico/cuixmala.html","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Goldsmith''s 25,000-acre biosphere estate — zebras, nesting turtles, private airstrip, total seclusion","si":"ultra","blurb":"Goldsmith''s 25,000-acre biosphere estate — zebras, nesting turtles, private airstrip, total seclusion","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"ocean":"destination","romance":"destination","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Las Alamandas","si_tag":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Las Alamandas direct / DMC","source":"https://www.alamandas.com/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"18 suites across 8 villas, plus 16% VAT / 3% room tax / 14% service. On application","si":"ultra","blurb":"18 suites across 8 villas, plus 16% VAT / 3% room tax / 14% service. On application","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"ocean":"destination","romance":"destination","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Careyes staffed-villa honeymoon","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Careyes reservations / villa specialist","source":"https://careyes.com/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"private staffed villa/casita with cook, cliff-and-cove privacy — a celebrity-wedding coast","si":"romance","blurb":"private staffed villa/casita with cook, cliff-and-cove privacy — a celebrity-wedding coast","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"ocean":"destination","romance":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"El Careyes Club & Residences","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"future","tier":"luxury","bookable":"Careyes reservations","source":"https://careyes.com/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"beachfront club stay for couples wanting hotel-style service inside the enclave","si":"romance","blurb":"beachfront club stay for couples wanting hotel-style service inside the enclave","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"ocean":"destination","romance":"primary","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Careyes polo - Agua Alta Cup (Easter)","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"premier","bookable":"Careyes events / villa package","source":"https://www.ondalinda.com/festivals/careyes/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the enclave''s signature spectacle, played Easter week; Chinese New Year tournament too","si":"ocean","blurb":"the enclave''s signature spectacle, played Easter week; Chinese New Year tournament too","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"on application","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["ocean"],"shelf_fit":{"ocean":"primary","romance":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Sailing + winter humpback coast","si_tag":"Ocean Adventures","status":"future","tier":"luxury","bookable":"charter / villa concierge (content-only)","source":"https://www.costalegre.ca/","hook":"sailing off the coves; humpbacks migrate Dec–Mar offshore","si":"ocean","blurb":"sailing off the coves; humpbacks migrate Dec–Mar offshore","commission":"operator (content-only)","wells":["move"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["ocean"],"shelf_fit":{"ocean":"primary","romance":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["operator"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"Can I book Careyes through TravelWell right now?","a":"No — Careyes is content-only today. Failing that named-carve-out gate sets book_enabled=FALSE.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Careyes?","a":"The road transfer, not the enclave itself. Ground transfers from Puerto Vallarta or Manzanillo run through non-carve-out southern Jalisco, and the advisory warns specifically against secondary highways after dark — this is the hold reason. The enclave is also remote: serious medical cases route ~1.5 hr to Manzanillo or 2–4 hr to Puerto Vallarta, so air-evac insurance is essential.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What makes Careyes so exclusive?","a":"It is a genuinely private, family-owned ultra node — not a resort. Founded in 1968, it pairs clifftop castles and ~50 staffed villas with two adjacent Goldsmith estates: Cuixmala, a ~25,000-acre biosphere reserve with its own airstrip, and Las Alamandas, an 18-suite gated boutique. All three have private airstrips — the crux of a possible future \"arrive-by-private-air\" clean pass.","source":"luxurylatinamerica.com / careyes.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ultra"},{"q":"Is Careyes good for a honeymoon or wedding?","a":"Yes — it is one of Mexico''s most cinematic private-wedding coasts. Heidi Klum and Seal married here, and the product is a fully staffed villa or casita with a private cook and total cliff-and-cove privacy, plus El Careyes Club & Residences for hotel-style service. Peak is the dry Nov–Apr season, and villas for that window contract 6–12 months ahead.","source":"careyes.com / aol.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is polo season and the Ondalinda festival?","a":"Professional polo runs late November to the end of April, with the marquee Agua Alta Cup played Easter week and a Chinese New Year tournament; the Ondalinda x Careyes festival is dated Nov 12–15, 2026. Winter also brings humpbacks offshore (Dec–Mar). Staffed-villa demand for these dates books 6–12 months out.","source":"ondalinda.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Careyes Mexico: Clifftop Castles, Polo & the Costalegre Ultra Coast","meta_description":"Careyes — Gian Franco Brignone''s 1968 private ultra enclave on Jalisco''s Costalegre: clifftop castles, staffed villas, polo, sailing, Ondalinda, plus Cuixmala & Las Alamandas.","slug":"careyes-mexico","primary_keyword":"Careyes Mexico","long_tail":["Careyes villas rent","Careyes clifftop castles","Careyes polo Agua Alta Cup","Ondalinda Careyes 2026","Cuixmala vs Careyes vs Las Alamandas","Careyes private airstrip access"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["Careyes Mexico","villas Careyes renta","castillos Careyes","polo Careyes Copa Agua Alta","Ondalinda Careyes 2026","Cuixmala reserva","Las Alamandas Costalegre"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-07-04","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_a